{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_story_01_search_flow_cache_aside", "label": "Cache-aside pattern (hand-written)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/story/01-search-flow.md", "source_location": "01-search-flow.md:120-155", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The application itself checks and writes the cache; the project plan explicitly bans the shortcut annotation (@Cacheable) so the pattern gets hand-written once as a learning exercise."}, {"id": "docs_story_01_search_flow_cache_key_correctness_rule", "label": "Cache-key correctness rule", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/story/01-search-flow.md", "source_location": "01-search-flow.md:279-320", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Whatever can change the upstream answer must be inside the hashed text, and whatever cannot must be left out. freshness is included even though unwired, because wiring it later would otherwise collide two different searches on one entry; maxResults and minTier are excluded because they are applied after the cache read and would force paying twice for byte-identical data."}, {"id": "docs_story_01_search_flow_hashing_is_tidiness_not_correctness", "label": "Hashing is tidiness, not correctness", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/story/01-search-flow.md", "source_location": "01-search-flow.md:295-310", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "SHA-256 exists only to give short, fixed-length, space-free and colon-free Redis keys. Correctness lives one step earlier, in what you feed the hasher."}, {"id": "docs_story_01_search_flow_key_versioning", "label": "Versioned key prefix (search:v1:searxng:)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/story/01-search-flow.md", "source_location": "01-search-flow.md:322-327", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Bumping v1 to v2 makes an entire generation of entries unreachable so they expire on their own - far safer than hunting down and deleting individual keys. The provider segment is hardcoded so a second provider later does not force a cache-wide bump."}, {"id": "docs_story_01_search_flow_stream_order_filter_before_limit", "label": "Filter before limit (stream stage order is meaning)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/story/01-search-flow.md", "source_location": "01-search-flow.md:509-560", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Trimming before judging would let low-quality blogs fill every slot and then be discarded, leaving far fewer results than asked for while excellent sources sat past the cut."}, {"id": "docs_story_01_search_flow_snippet_rename", "label": "content renamed to snippet at the API boundary", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/story/01-search-flow.md", "source_location": "01-search-flow.md:520-528", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "content is the search engine's word; snippet is ours. The public API should not inherit somebody else's vocabulary."}, {"id": "docs_story_01_search_flow_cache_stampede", "label": "Cache stampede / thundering herd", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/story/01-search-flow.md", "source_location": "01-search-flow.md:713-760", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Nothing throws and no test fails - it is pure waste. Six concurrent threads compute the same key, all miss, all fetch, all write, all spend. The cache only helps after somebody finishes."}, {"id": "docs_story_01_search_flow_single_flight_lock", "label": "Single-flight lock (planned, unbuilt)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/story/01-search-flow.md", "source_location": "01-search-flow.md:748-760", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The first thread claims a short-lived marker with Redis's atomic set-if-absent and is the only one allowed to fetch; the others wait briefly and re-read. Deliberately deferred as a hand-written exercise."}, {"id": "docs_story_01_search_flow_no_error_handling", "label": "No error handling anywhere in the search flow", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/story/01-search-flow.md", "source_location": "01-search-flow.md:640-712", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Neither the controller nor SearchService contains a try/catch, so every failure surfaces as a bare HTTP 500. Acceptable at this stage, but known on purpose rather than by surprise. Notable ordering effect: a negative maxResults throws only after the fetch, cache write and credit spend have already happened."}, {"id": "docs_story_01_search_flow_expiry_is_the_only_cleanup", "label": "Everything expires on its own (no cleanup job)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/story/01-search-flow.md", "source_location": "01-search-flow.md:762-770", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Cache entries and the quota counter carry their own 24h TTL and failed operations wrote nothing, so there is no cron, sweeper or cleanup task at all."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_story_01_search_flow_cache_aside", "target": "docs_story_00_the_world_searchservice", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/story/01-search-flow.md", "source_location": "01-search-flow.md:150-155", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_story_01_search_flow_cache_key_correctness_rule", "target": "docs_story_01_search_flow_hashing_is_tidiness_not_correctness", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/story/01-search-flow.md", "source_location": "01-search-flow.md:295-320", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_story_01_search_flow_hashing_is_tidiness_not_correctness", "target": "docs_story_00_the_world_hashing", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/story/01-search-flow.md", "source_location": "01-search-flow.md:295-310", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_story_01_search_flow_key_versioning", "target": "docs_story_01_search_flow_cache_aside", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/story/01-search-flow.md", "source_location": "01-search-flow.md:322-327", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_story_01_search_flow_cache_key_correctness_rule", "target": "docs_story_00_the_world_searchservice", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/story/01-search-flow.md", "source_location": "01-search-flow.md:279-320", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_story_01_search_flow_stream_order_filter_before_limit", "target": "docs_story_00_the_world_sourcetierresolver", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/story/01-search-flow.md", "source_location": "01-search-flow.md:509-560", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_story_01_search_flow_snippet_rename", "target": "docs_story_03_extract_stub_flow_field_names_are_the_contract", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/story/01-search-flow.md", "source_location": "01-search-flow.md:520-528", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_story_01_search_flow_cache_stampede", "target": "docs_story_01_search_flow_single_flight_lock", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/story/01-search-flow.md", "source_location": "01-search-flow.md:748-760", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_story_01_search_flow_cache_stampede", "target": "docs_story_01_search_flow_cache_aside", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/story/01-search-flow.md", "source_location": "01-search-flow.md:713-747", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_story_01_search_flow_no_error_handling", "target": "docs_story_00_the_world_searchservice", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/story/01-search-flow.md", "source_location": "01-search-flow.md:640-650", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_story_01_search_flow_expiry_is_the_only_cleanup", "target": "docs_story_02_quota_flow_ttl_is_the_cleaner", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/story/01-search-flow.md", "source_location": "01-search-flow.md:762-770", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_story_01_search_flow_cache_aside", "target": "docs_story_00_the_world_searxng", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/story/01-search-flow.md", "source_location": "01-search-flow.md:430-470", "weight": 1.0}], "hyperedges": [{"id": "search_flow_participants", "label": "The search flow end to end", "nodes": ["docs_story_00_the_world_retrievalcontroller", "docs_story_00_the_world_searchservice", "docs_story_00_the_world_redis", "docs_story_00_the_world_searxng", "docs_story_00_the_world_quotaservice", "docs_story_00_the_world_sourcetierresolver", "docs_story_01_search_flow_cache_aside"], "relation": "participate_in", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/story/01-search-flow.md"}, {"id": "versioned_cache_key_discipline", "label": "Versioned, canonicalized cache-key discipline", "nodes": ["docs_story_01_search_flow_cache_key_correctness_rule", "docs_story_01_search_flow_hashing_is_tidiness_not_correctness", "docs_story_01_search_flow_key_versioning", "docs_story_00_the_world_hashing", "docs_story_00_the_world_urlnormalizer", "docs_story_